From af15e4385d11574b501739dc3347380f804ed459 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kimi Chen <kimi.zy.chen@fii-foxconn.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Jan 2026 12:16:45 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 3003/3003] Ignore smbpbi sensor event report

During the AC cycle or reboot, after the power state changes to "on",
we observed numerous event reports from Smbpbi sensors. We will
temporarily ignore the event reporting for smbpbi sensors and track
the cause of the event reporting.

Signed-off-by: Kimi Chen <kimi.zy.chen@fii-foxconn.com>
---
 src/sensor.hpp | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/sensor.hpp b/src/sensor.hpp
index c865703..a3a8513 100644
--- a/src/sensor.hpp
+++ b/src/sensor.hpp
@@ -284,7 +284,9 @@ struct Sensor
             // Manager config), these sensors are expected to become invalid,
             // and we will ignore their sensor event reporting. This helps avoid
             // seeing redundant sensor events during power operations.
-            if (!readingStateGood())
+            if (!readingStateGood() ||
+                configInterface ==
+                    "xyz.openbmc_project.Configuration.SmbpbiVirtualEeprom")
             {
                 return 1;
             }
-- 
